  "packageSize": 115155,
  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "releaseNotes": "6.33.0 — ADDITIVE: TWO new ApplicationAdminPermission members, 232 RestoreUser and 233 EraseUser (bg-identity#113, recoverable account deletion). RestoreUser reverses an administrator soft delete; EraseUser is the irreversible erasure of an already soft-deleted account. APPENDED AT THE END as the freeze contract requires: ApplicationAdminPermissionFreezeTests was taken RED first (2 of 2: the count and the name/value collection) and green only after the append; the committed catalogue is REGENERATED, not edited. Shared owns the names and ordinals; bg-identity owns the default-role distribution. Consumers re-pin to 6.33.0; existing principals receive no personal grant from the enum growing - admins grant them (owner rule). Nothing existing changed. PREVIOUSLY, 6.32.0 — ADDITIVE: TWO new ApplicationAdminPermission members, 230 RestorePresentation and 231 PurgePresentation (bg-usercontent#53). They keep reversible recovery and delete-forever separate from DeletePresentation. Owner decision 2026-09-29: ContentManager receives RestorePresentation but NOT PurgePresentation; SuperAdmin and SuperModerator receive both; no other default role receives either. APPENDED AT THE END so every existing ordinal remains unchanged. The catalogue is regenerated from the enum. Consumers must re-pin; Identity must seed the approved default-role map, while grants for already-assigned principals remain a separately measured and authorized data change. Full prior notes remain in docs/CHANGELOG.md.",
